# Factory rules

This repo runs the software factory. Read `.factory/FACTORY.md` and `.factory/skills/local-open-weights-run.md` before you act.

## "do issue N"

1. Run `gh issue view N --comments`. The issue and its comments are the scope.
2. Run `bash scripts/factory-cost.sh start N` before any other work.
3. Follow `.factory/skills/factory-loop.md`: sync the default branch, branch `issue-N-<slug>`, build, self-review, open the PR with `Closes #N`.
4. Stay in Agent mode. Change only the files the issue lists. Don't create files it doesn't ask for.
5. After the PR is open, run `bash scripts/factory-cost.sh end N` and put its `Cost:` and `Caching:` lines in the PR body.

## "address the review on PR N"

Follow the **Fixes** step in `.factory/skills/local-open-weights-run.md`: read the latest `Factory review` comment, fix each numbered item, push to the same branch, and reply on the PR item by item.

## Report honestly

- Tick a box only when the diff or a command's output proves it. Otherwise leave it unticked and write "not done" with the reason.
- Don't claim a test ran unless you show its output.

## Never

- Never merge (`gh pr merge`), never push to `main`, never force push.
- Never use `--no-verify` or `FACTORY_ALLOW_MAIN_PUSH`.
- Never print env vars or keys (`env`, `printenv`, `echo $KEY`, `cat ~/.zshrc`).
- Never run `curl` or `gh api` yourself; scripts in `scripts/` do the API calls.
